{"file":"prove-0.2.0-v2.zip","bytes":59816,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"prove","description":"Measure-before-you-ship discipline for Claude Code: a methodology skill, an experiment-reviewer agent, and a drop-in benchmark harness scaffold.","version":"0.2.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/VassilisSoum/prove","homepage":"https://github.com/VassilisSoum/prove","keywords":["claude-code","plugin","benchmarking","evaluation","scientific-method","ab-testing","verification"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/empirical-method/SKILL.md","name":"empirical-method","description":"Measure a change before you ship it. Use this skill BEFORE claiming an improvement, optimization, or fix works — and before approving, merging, or shipping a behavior change. It installs a falsifiable loop: hypothesis → isolate one lever → fair floor baseline at equal budget → score on the real outcome (not a proxy) → enough trials for the variance → keep only on measured benefit, else revert → record the result (incl. negatives) durably. Trigger whenever you catch yourself saying \"this is faster / better / fixes it\" without a number, when tuning a parameter or swapping a model/algorithm/prompt, or when asked to evaluate or benchmark anything.","headings":["The empirical method","When this applies","The loop","Falsifiability — name the kill condition up front","Anti-patterns (each one fools you into shipping noise)","How to run it"],"name_hint":"empirical · method"},{"path":"skills/scaffold-benchmark/SKILL.md","name":"scaffold-benchmark","description":"Measure a proposed change for the developer — author and run the experiment, don't hand them a blank template. Use when someone asks \"is X better?\", \"should I ship this?\", \"did this improve Y?\", or proposes swapping/tuning an implementation. Reads the change from the code (git diff / the named functions), scaffolds the bench/ harness if absent, WRITES the arms + a starter case set (including adversarial cases) by reading the repo, shows the cases for a quick human OK, runs it, and reports the verdict. The developer's whole job is: ask the question, eyeball the cases, read the result.","headings":["Measure a change (author + run the experiment)","The flow","The contract every port must preserve","What stays the developer's call"],"name_hint":"scaffold · 对标"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["prove","What's in the box","When should I use Prove?","The loop","Install","from anywhere","Verify your install","Quickstart (the harness, standalone)","Example: using it in a project","Outcome vs numeric metrics","Using Prove with Pull Requests","Design notes","Why these rules","Known limitations"]},{"path":"templates/bench/README.md","headings":["`bench/` — the prove harness","The contract (3 files, 1 of which you edit)","Run it","The four rules the harness enforces for you","Defining your experiment (`registry.py`)","Reading the result","Don't fool yourself","Other languages"]},{"path":"examples/numeric-cost/README.md","headings":["Example: numeric-cost","Run it","What you'll see"]},{"path":"examples/simple-ranking/README.md","headings":["Example: simple-ranking","The setup","Run it","What you'll see"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".github/workflows/ci.yml",".gitignore","LICENSE","README.md","agents/experimentalist.md","examples/numeric-cost/README.md","examples/numeric-cost/bench/EXPERIMENTS.md","examples/numeric-cost/bench/registry.py","examples/numeric-cost/bench/results/.gitkeep","examples/numeric-cost/bench/run.py","examples/numeric-cost/bench/score.py","examples/numeric-cost/cost.py","examples/numeric-cost/expected_output.txt","examples/simple-ranking/README.md","examples/simple-ranking/bench/EXPERIMENTS.md","examples/simple-ranking/bench/registry.py","examples/simple-ranking/bench/results/.gitkeep","examples/simple-ranking/bench/run.py","examples/simple-ra